    {
      "title": "Monolith vs Microservices: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Monolith vs Microservices: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Shapes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Monolith}: ==one deployable==, one codebase, one database",
                "Module calls are **in-process** functions: fast, transactional",
                "{purple:Microservices}: many small, ==independently deployable== services",
                "Each owns one **business capability** and its own data",
                "Services talk over the **network**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Trade",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Monolith",
                "Microservices"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Deploy",
                  "All-or-nothing",
                  "Per service"
                ],
                [
                  "Scaling",
                  "Whole app",
                  "Per service"
                ],
                [
                  "Tech stack",
                  "One",
                  "Polyglot"
                ],
                [
                  "Debugging",
                  "One stack trace",
                  "Distributed tracing"
                ],
                [
                  "Transactions",
                  "ACID",
                  "Sagas"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Core trade",
              "text": "Microservices swap {blue:code complexity} for ==distributed-systems complexity==: network failures, latency, partial failure, eventual consistency."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Modular Monolith",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One deployable== with strict **module boundaries**",
                "Usually the best **starting point**",
                "Cheap path to split later: a module becomes a service"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Modular monolith",
                    "sub": "strict boundaries",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pick a module",
                    "sub": "own data, clean API",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Extract it",
                    "sub": "deploy separately",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Microservice",
                    "sub": "over the network",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Service Boundaries and Database per Service",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Service Boundaries and Database per Service",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Drawing the Boundary",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Split by",
                "Example",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Business capability",
                  "Orders, Payments, Inventory",
                  "{green:Good}"
                ],
                [
                  "Technical layer",
                  "UI, DB, logic",
                  "{red:Bad}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bounded context== (DDD) = one business capability",
                "Test: a typical change touches ==one service==",
                "Test: it deploys with ==no coordination== with others"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Database per Service",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each service ==owns its schema==",
                "Others use its ==API or events==, never its tables",
                "Reporting: ==events or a read model==, no cross-service joins",
                "Consistency: ==saga== plus eventual consistency, not distributed 2PC"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Saga: place an order",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Create order",
                    "note": "local transaction",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Charge payment",
                    "note": "local transaction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reserve stock fails",
                    "note": "local transaction",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Refund payment",
                    "note": "compensating action",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Classic Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Shared database between services",
                "Distributed monolith: services must deploy together",
                "Chatty calls to serve one request"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Boundary smell",
              "text": "One change that needs edits and deploys in ==several services== means the boundary is wrong."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Service Discovery and Sync vs Async Calls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Service Discovery and Sync vs Async Calls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Service Discovery",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Instances come and go with ==autoscaling==",
                "Callers look up ==healthy addresses by service name==",
                "Registry: {blue:Consul}, {blue:Eureka}",
                "Platform DNS: {purple:Kubernetes Service name}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Client-side",
                "Server-side"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Resolves",
                  "Caller queries registry",
                  "LB or proxy"
                ],
                [
                  "Balancing",
                  "Caller does it",
                  "Proxy does it"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sync vs Async",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Sync (REST, gRPC)",
                "Async (Kafka, RabbitMQ, SQS)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Caller",
                  "Waits for reply",
                  "Publishes, moves on"
                ],
                [
                  "Pro",
                  "Simple, immediate",
                  "Decouples, absorbs spikes"
                ],
                [
                  "Con",
                  "Couples availability and latency",
                  "Eventual consistency, duplicates, hard debugging"
                ],
                [
                  "Availability",
                  "==Product== of each service's",
                  "Independent"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Producer",
                    "sub": "publishes",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "queue or topic",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Consumer",
                    "sub": "idempotent",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "==Sync== for queries needing an immediate answer. ==Async== for commands and events that trigger follow-up work."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Client-side vs server-side discovery?** Caller queries and balances itself; a proxy does it for the caller.",
                "**Why is a sync chain fragile?** Availability multiplies: three 99.9% services give about 99.7%.",
                "**Async downside?** Duplicate delivery, so make consumers idempotent."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Timeouts and Resilience",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Timeouts and Resilience",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Timeouts on every call",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Set a ==timeout on every remote call==",
                "Default is often {red:infinite}: one slow dependency eats all threads, **outage cascades**",
                "Base it on the dependency's observed ==p99 latency==",
                "Caller timeout **>** callee timeout; total fits the user deadline"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "requests.get(url, timeout=(1, 2))"
              ],
              "note": "connect 1s, read 2s"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Retries and circuit breaker",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Retry only ==idempotent== calls",
                "Exponential ==backoff + jitter==, capped retry count",
                "Unbounded retries cause a {red:retry storm}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Closed",
                    "sub": "calls pass",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Open",
                    "sub": "after N failures, fail fast",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Half-open",
                    "sub": "one probe call",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Closed",
                    "sub": "probe ok",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Bulkhead and fallback",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Bulkhead",
              "items": [
                "Separate thread or connection pool **per dependency**",
                "A slow dependency fills only its own pool"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always define a fallback",
              "text": "Return ==cached data== or a **degraded response** when the call fails, times out, or the breaker is open."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Service Mesh and Sidecars",
      "role": "outline",
